  "contract": "Issue #7361: on Ascension a Worldforged item climbed past its first upgrade at the Guardian of Time (custom stores 8 and 9, CMSG 0x6BB {u32 key, u32 quantity}, SMSG 0x6BC result string) once the account had killed a raid's last boss: Hakkar opened the next tier for every character of the account, then Ragnaros, then Onyxia (reported by the user). The unlock is kept per account, so a character of another account stays locked; a second character of the same account is not driven here because two sessions of one account share its extension packet queue. Each tier is a fixed item-id offset from the first-rank item: Rusty Blunderbuss 1378061 (ilvl 64) upgrades to 1380061 (ilvl 70) after Hakkar and to 1392061 (ilvl 73) after Ragnaros. The prices are computed, not recovered: tier n costs the first upgrade's price times 1 + 0.5 (n - 1), so 5000 Runes of Ascension becomes 7500 for tier 2. A locked purchase names the boss and takes nothing.",
